From: Daniel Richard G. <skunk@iskunk.org>
Subject: Fix WASI libc++ link errors

Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2033572

The libc++ of Ubuntu for wasm32 is built with C++ exceptions, but its
libc++abi does not define them, so the RLBox sandboxes fail to link.

From patches/no-exceptions.patch of the Firefox snap
(https://github.com/canonical/firefox-snap, branch stable).

G Unity⁷: also define __cxa_begin_catch, which the libc++ of LLVM 22 in
Ubuntu 26.10 needs. Hunk offset refreshed for Firefox 159.
---
--- a/memory/mozalloc/mozalloc.cpp
+++ b/memory/mozalloc/mozalloc.cpp
@@ -153,3 +153,13 @@
   return 0;
 #endif
 }
+
+#if defined(__wasm32__)
+extern "C"
+{
+  void *__cxa_allocate_exception(size_t)    { abort(); }
+  void  __cxa_throw(void *, void *, void *) { abort(); }
+  void  __cxa_rethrow()                     { abort(); }
+  void *__cxa_begin_catch(void *)           { abort(); }
+}
+#endif
